Thanks for your quick response. You are right. We are repeating a survey with same survey design, where they got around 4,5% overlap in the first one, so I am expecting something similar for this second survey... I guess that if I deal with the double-counting observation at corners (driven then just to one of the lines), not taking into account the overlap areas would not introduce significant bias to the results being small %...

