Dear Eric:

Do you think we should still assume population closure when estimating densities using camera trap distance sampling (CTDS). But I did not find the dsecriptions and assumptions about the population closure in the published articals about CTDS (Apologies if I missed it). When estimating the species with low densities, we should using data covering longer periods to get enough detections to get a better fit about detetion probibilities, but the longer periods might violate the assumptions of the population closure. If the population is not enclosed, can we still use CTDS? Thank you!

cheers,

Zhilin Li

